## Development Conventions

- Branch from `main`: `feat/...`, `fix/...`, `refactor/...`
- Commits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`, `docs:`
- All prompts in `.md` files, not hardcoded in Python
- SOLID principles: SRP services, DI via bot_data, BaseTool abstraction
- Test locally via `./start_devtest.sh` before PR
- Deploy via `./deploy.sh` to Cloud Run

## Guardrails for Student Content

- Answers MUST align with CBSE curriculum (subject codes: AI 417, CS 083, IT 402, IP 065)
- Auto-detect answer format: explain vs board-exam style (1/2/3/5 mark)
- Always cite sources: chapter, PDF name, video title with timestamp
- Socratic method for conceptual questions (guide, don't just give answer)
- Age-appropriate content filtering (Classes 10-12, ages 15-18)
- No direct exam answers -- teach understanding, then model answer

## Workflow: Which Tool for What

- **Starting a phase:** GSD (`gsd-discuss-phase` -> `gsd-plan-phase` -> `gsd-execute-phase` -> `gsd-verify-work`)
- **Complex feature inside a phase:** feature-dev (7-phase: discover -> explore -> clarify -> architect -> implement -> review -> summary)
- **Need a PRD first:** PM skill `pm-create-prd`
- **Quick fix:** `gsd-fast`
- **Small task with some structure:** `gsd-quick`
- **Don't know which command:** `gsd-do` (describe in plain English)
- **Lost context:** Read this file (auto-loaded) + `V0-PROJECT-BIBLE.md` Section 16 + `gsd-resume-work`
- **Prioritize features:** `pm-prioritize-features`
- **Define student personas:** `pm-user-personas`
- **Set up metrics:** `pm-metrics-dashboard`
- **Debug a problem:** `gsd-debug`

